# netsurf (vita frontend): image textures from a pooled allocator (texpool); consent-wall cookies
#
# - Hardware run 18: vita2d_create_empty_texture gives every image its own
#   kernel memory block -- one kernel object (UID) each, rounded up to 256 KB
#   of CDRAM. Image-heavy browsing ran the process out of UIDs; from then on
#   every DNS lookup failed at once with SCE_KERNEL_ERROR_UID_RL_OVERFLOW
#   (0x8002450D) and sites "did not open at all" (adverts.ie, gmail.com,
#   even lite.cnn.com, which had loaded earlier). Bitmaps now come from 8 MB
#   arenas (vita/texpool.c: one memblock each, CDRAM else uncached main,
#   mapped for the GPU once; 1 KB granular), wrapped with
#   sceGxmTextureInitLinear. Frees wait for the frame the GPU is drawing
#   (vita_bitmap_frame_retired after vita2d_wait_rendering_done), replacing
#   a full GPU wait per destroyed image. log.txt: "bitmaps: N live, KB in
#   arenas, refused" at each load's end. texpool.c was written by the local
#   pi agent (work order T1; 10 host checks incl. a 200000-op soak under
#   ASan/UBSan) and reviewed; one bug fixed (arena_push's failure path
#   decremented a count it had not incremented).
# - Google's and YouTube's cookie-consent walls: seed their answer, SOCS=CAI
#   ("Reject all"), for .google.com / .youtube.com / .google.ie /
#   .google.co.uk unless the jar already has one.
